New Predator Types
Choosing a Predator Type is one of the most
important aspects of character creation in V5. It
sets the tone of your vampire's nightly existence
and relationship with their Beast, it grants you
Disciplines to which you might not otherwise have
access, and it offers new characters and other seeds
for your Storyteller to nourish into plot.
The V5 Core Rulebook offered ten
Predator Types to begin with, and several more
have been released since. Here, we describe 24
completely new Predator Types for you to choose
from during character creation. Each new
Predator Type offers a unique combination of
Disciplines and a flavorful array of skill specialties
and Advantages. They are particularly helpful to
the Storyteller, for whom reusing the same dozen
Predator Types in non­player characters can get a
little repetitive.
As with all Predator Types, choosing one
of the styles given here does not force you to feed
only in that manner. Unless the Predator Type
imposes a Flaw that restricts feeding, you are free
to feed in other ways without consequence,
allowing you to adapt to the resources available on
any given night.

Ambulance Chaser

Humans shed blood all the time ­ in car accidents,
drive­by shootings, domestic stabbings, and any of
a myriad of weirder and rarer circumstances. You
wait for these moments of bloody serendipity,
pouncing on the victims to lick up the blood that
flows from their wounds before the other first
responders can arrive. Perhaps you even turn into
an animal ­ a stray dog, a crow, or maybe even a
vulture ­ to make the feeding less remarkable.
Maybe it's a little cold­blooded of you to take
advantage of people already in a bad state, but hey,
you weren't the one to hurt them. Maybe you even
administer first aid once you've drunk your fill! In
life, you might have been an adrenaline junky, a
first­responder, or a true crime enthusiast.
• Add a specialty: Drive (Emergency
Vehicles) or Medicine (First Aid)
• Gain one dot of Potence or Protean
• Spend three dots between Influence,
Contacts, and Allies (•••)
• Gain the Obvious Predator Flaw (••)

• Hunting Pools: Manipulation + Medicine
or Wits + Larceny. Once you've found a site
with wounded mortals, either disguise your
collection of blood samples as medically
necessary or lap up the blood when no
one's
looking.

Blood Baby

You don't have to bother with finding ways to
slake your hunger ­ an older and more powerful
vampire takes care of that for you. Your Mawla
lets you feed from their Herd, caters mortals for
your nightly sustenance, or allows you to access
their stockpile of bagged blood. Add your Mawla
to the relationship map. The Storyteller will make
sure your Mawla has Merits that allow them to
provide you with blood regularly. You might have
been a child when you were Embraced, or you
might have been a trust fund baby, an orphan, or
an artist.
• Add a specialty: Persuasion (Begging) or
Technology (Catfishing)
• Gain one dot of Presence or Dominate
• Gain the Mawla Merit (••)
• Gain the Disliked Flaw (•) Some Kindred
look down on you for being unable or
unwilling to hunt for yourself.
• Hunting Pools: Manipulation + Persuasion
or Charisma + Technology. Call up your
Mawla
and wheedle them into sending you a snack or ­
when you can't do that ­ catfish
some bozo off
the internet for a quick
meetup. Sure, he
might be a predator ­ but
so are you.

Codependent

Hunting? You don't know her. You feed from a
single mortal exclusively: your partner, parent,
best friend, or trusted servant. This mortal ­ your
blood doll ­ likely accompanies you everywhere, in
case the Hunger should take you. They live in
constant danger of your loss of control over the
Beast, but you treat them well ­ you must, or
they'll decline within a week from pernicious
anemia, and you will be left with no way to sate
your Hunger. Most Kindred with this predator
type are overprotective and attentive to their blood
doll's needs, plying them with orange juice,
cookies, and iron supplements after each feeding,
and protecting them from danger with their own

undead flesh. Your Humanity might suffer if your
blood doll dies, but you can replace them given
time to form a bond with someone new. You could
have come from any background, but you probably
had an unusually strong bond ­ possibly to an
unhealthy degree ­ with the mortal that now
supports you as your blood doll.
• Add a specialty: Etiquette (Blood Dolls)
or Medicine (Anemia)
• Gain one dot of Dominate or Fortitude
• Gain a three­dot Retainer (•••) (your
blood doll)
• Gain the Feeding Flaw: Dependent (••)
• Hunting Pools: Charisma + Etiquette or
Intelligence + Medicine. There's little
chance
of being unable to feed on your
dedicated
blood doll, but you need to keep
them healthy
and happy by treating them respectfully and
tending to them medically after feeding.

Condiment King

You don't just drink blood ­ you eat it. You prefer
to take your meals by mixing blood with mortal
food. Maybe you just dip your French fries in a
side of A­positive, or maybe you prepare fine
meals laced throughout with raw blood chosen
meticulously for its resonance and antigenicity.
Either way, you use only the freshest of
ingredients; the blood you consume must still be
fresh when it is applied to your solid meals (unless
you gained the Iron Gullet Merit separately). In
life, you might have been a chef, a foodie, a college
student, or a stay­at­home parent.
• Add a specialty: Craft (Cooking) or
Etiquette (Table Manners)
• Gain one dot of Auspex or Protean
• Gain the Mythic Merit: Eat Food (••)
• Gain the Mythic Flaw: Folkloric Block
(Garlic) (•)
• Hunting Pools: Wits + Craft or
Manipulation + Etiquette. Gain access to fresh
blood (usually animal blood) under the cover of
preparing a fine meal or
beguile a mortal at a
high society dinner with your excellent table
manners ­ and use
their blood as a condiment
for the leftovers.

the disabled an easy way to make a living, the
terminally ill a way to extend their life, the
depressed a convenient means of simplifying their
responsibilities. Perhaps you even trick yourself
into believing that your freely­entered contracts
make your feeding moral, consensual ­ you and
your vessels just try not to think about the
impossibility of your prosecution if you ever did
violate the terms of the agreement. In life, you
might have been an attorney, a salesperson, a drug
lord, or a corporate hiring manager.
• Add a specialty: Academics (Law) or
Streetwise (Bribes)
• Gain one dot of Auspex or Presence
• Gain three dots of Herd (•••) (they are
Blood Bonded to you if you choose to make that a
term of their contracts)
• Gain the Adversary Flaw (••) (a Kindred
that sees your feeding activities as exploitation
or Masquerade breach)
• Hunting Pools: Intelligence + Academics
or Resolve + Streetwise. Weave dizzying legal
jargon around your prey until they sign their
blood away to you or make a binding handshake
deal with someone off
the street too scared
by your eating habits and enamored of your
money to squeal.

Delivery Diner

Modern nights bring modern solutions to the
ancient demands of the Beast. You prefer to feed
under the cover of delivery ­ you order takeout
and take a few pints out of the driver as an extra
on the ticket, or you are the driver, feeding on poor
mortals ordering sad Chinese for one. You might
have been a delivery driver in life, a hustler, or
nearly any other kind of person.
• Add a specialty: Technology (Apps) or
Drive (Trucks)
• Gain one dot of Dominate or Obfuscate
• Gain a dot of Haven or Resources (•)
• Hunting Pools: Intelligence + Technology
or Wits + Drive. Use an "app," as the
youth
call them, to order a delivery driver sent straight
to your home or park your work vehicle
strategically to obscure view while you feed on the
recipients of your
deliveries.

Contractor

Like the silver­tongued devil himself, you
specialize in beguiling or ensnaring victims into
contractual agreements for their blood. You seek
out the vulnerable to make your offers: promising

Incarcerator

You kidnap and imprison your victims in your

Haven, to feed on over the course of months or
even years. If you're smart, you are careful to fake
their deaths, allaying suspicions and diverting law
enforcement. Many incarcerators prefer to
imprison those who they feel deserve this fate:
violent criminals, abusive parents, human
traffickers, police officers, etc. In life, you might
have suffered at the hands of the type of mortal
you now target for kidnapping, or you could have
been law enforcement or military.
• Add a specialty: Brawl (Kidnapping) or
Larceny (Falsifying Crime Scenes)
• Gain one dot of Potence or Oblivion
• Gain a two­dot Haven (••)
• Gain one dot of the Haven: Cells Merit(•)
• Gain two dots of the Enemies Flaw (••)
(escaped victims or law enforcement on the case)
• Hunting Pools: Dexterity + Brawl or
Intelligence + Larceny. Snatch someone off
the streets and spirit them into a cell in
your
haven or undertake meticulous
falsification of
an easy kidnappee's abduction site, faking a death
that leaves no body.

Intermittent Faster

You're not too picky about where your blood
comes from; you just try to drink as little as
possible. You fast for long stretches between meals,
trying to limit the burden you impose on the
world's mortals. Some Kindred with this predator
type seek enlightenment through pursuit of
Golconda, while others may hold fast to their
mortal faith and its moral restrictions.
• Add a specialty: Athletics (Endurance) or
Occult (Golconda)
• Gain one dot of Animalism or Fortitude
• Gain the Intermittent Fasting feeding
Flaw (••)
• Gain a dot of Humanity
• Hunting Pools: You sate your Hunger
opportunistically or when the Beast can be
controlled no longer. When you are forced to
hunt, you do so in the easiest way that
comes
to mind; use any dice pool you can justify to your
Storyteller.

Maskless

"Hide in plain sight," has always been your motto.
You prefer to feed while being observed by an
audience of hundreds, if not thousands, of rapt

mortals, relying on incredulity to convince them
that you surely cannot actually be drinking human
blood. You star in vampire movies and feed in front
of the camera, perform in a gothic stage show that
features dramatic "blood drinking" that surely must
be faked, or you run a channel for "sanguinarians"
that want to believe you're actually drinking blood
on stream ­ but as a kink, of course, not for basic
sustenance. Perhaps you make it easier for your
audience to rationalize by limiting your on­screen
activities to animal blood. You believe in the
Masquerade ­ really, you do! But you find it so
much more convenient to just allow the mortals to
convince themselves. The Camarilla, and many
other Kindred besides, don't agree with you, but
you have plenty of practice dealing with them. In
life, you might have been an actor, a stage
magician, a social media influencer, or a politician.
• Add a specialty: Performance (Drinking
Blood) or Politics (Masquerade)
• Gain one dot of Animalism or Presence
• Spend three dots between Fame and Mask
(•••)
• Spend two dots between the Infamy and
Suspect/Shunned Flaws (••)
• Hunting Pools: Manipulation +
Performance. Stage a show that involves
miming or actually drinking blood.

Opportunist

You feed on those on the fringes of society:
immigrants, the homeless, eccentrics, etc.
Mastering languages helps you to blend in with
diverse or immigrant communities as you hunt for
the gullible, naïve, and lonely. You offer a friendly
ear, an understanding presence, and you take just a
bit of blood in exchange. You might have come
from one of these communities when you were
alive, or you might have been a social worker, a
police officer, or an immigration official.
• Add a specialty: Streetwise (Cast­outs) or
Investigation (Immigrants)
• Gain one dot of Presence of Obfuscate
• Gain the Linguistics Merit (••)
• Gain the No Haven Flaw (•)
• Hunting Pools: Charisma + Streetwise or
Wits + Investigation. Ingratiate yourself
with someone living on the street and lure them
to a secluded location or track down an isolated
immigrant living alone – no one
to call the
cops when a predator appears at
their window.

Parasite

You feed on blood second­ or third­hand, plucking
ticks from bushes, lice from scalps, or mosquitoes
directly from the air. Not the most practical or
dignified of feeding styles, but there are rumors of
powerful Parasites that master swarms of vampire
bats or mosquitoes, casting them out into the night
air to feed and return to their master with blood.
Others simply feel that this disgusting indignity is
what they deserve as monsters leeching off the
blood of others. In life, you might have been an
entomologist, a charity worker, or an abnormal
psychologist.
• Add a specialty: Animal Ken (Swarms) or
Awareness (Blood Suckers)
• Gain one dot of Animalism or Celerity
• Gain a one­dot Mawla (•) (a Kindred
who
shares your feeding style or
supports you)
• Gain two dots of Retainers (••) (ghouled
animals)
• Gain the Obvious Predator Flaw (••)
• Hunting Pools: Manipulation + Animal
Ken or Dexterity + Awareness. If you have Feral
Whispers, you can use that to
dispatch a
swarm of blood­sucking
creatures into the
night to feed and return
to regurgitate the
blood into your mouth.
If not, spend hours
collecting ticks or
mosquitoes, each one a tiny
pinprick
of
disgusting satiation.

Quiverfull

You prefer to feed on your own childer rather than
on mortals. You have given the Embrace freely,
siring a coven of childer like a brood of children.
This family you have created serves as proxy for
your own feeding; your childer drain blood from
the wider world and make it available to you from
their veins. Some 13th generation Nosferatu or
Hecata have been known to Embrace a brood of
thin­bloods, free of the curse of their sire's clan,
using them to funnel blood into the sire's hideous
or deadly maw. If the Embrace is regulated in your
domain, you must either take the Infamy flaw for
having created so many illegal childer, or you must
have an explanation for why your large brood is
permitted. In life, you might have followed a
conservative faith or been a cult leader, a vampire
fanatic, or someone with a large found family.
• Add a specialty: Leadership (Childer) or
Academics (a religion of your choice)
• Gain one dot of Presence or Oblivion

• Lose one dot of Humanity
• Gain the Bond Resistance Merit (•••)
• Gain three 2­dot Mawla groups (••••••)
(your neonate childer)
• Gain the Living In the Past or Infamy
Flaw (•)
• Hunting Pools: Manipulation + Leadership
or Charisma + Academics. Appeal to your
childer's devotion to you or to the twisted faith
you've instilled in them to donate their
vitae
for your Hunger. Increase the
Difficulty by
your Bane Severity if you're Hecata ­ that shit
hurts.

Recycler

Your feeding habits are shaped by your rare
condition as an organovore. You eat human organs,
often sourced from bagged medical waste or from
corpses you dissect under cover as a mortician or
autopsy technician. These are resources that
mortals would fix with environmentally­harmful
chemicals or simply discard, so you believe that
you are doing the world a service by giving these
cast­off pieces of human life a new purpose. The
curse of the organovore strikes indiscriminately ­
at least as far as most Kindred can determine ­ so
almost anyone could develop this predator type.
• Add a specialty: Science (Anatomy) or
Subterfuge (Impersonation)
• Gain one dot of Protean or Oblivion
• Spend three dots between Contacts and
Mask (•••)
• Gain the Feeding Flaw: Organovore (••)
• Hunting Pools: Resolve + Science or
Manipulation + Subterfuge. Push through a
forensic examination and devour the
bagged organs once you're finally left alone and
off­camera or pass yourself off as a tech
authorized to dispose of a hospital's medical
waste.

Regulator

The blood is everything, but for you, it is emotion
most especially. You know how to attune your body
and mind to the resonance that you consume from
a vessel, regulating your own emotions with the
echoes of mortal feeling that you imbibe. Mortals
whose blood carries resonance are often in the
throes of intense emotion, distracted and easily fed
upon without breaking the Masquerade.
Regulators have a unique ability to manage the
Beast through careful choice of vessels, but your

dependence on blood with a resonance ­ often
difficult to locate in the thronging of lesser pulses
­ makes you susceptible to a hard crash when you
no longer have others' emotions to use as a crutch.
As a mortal, you might have had a mood disorder
or been a counselor, a gut microbiologist, or a
naturopath.
• Add a specialty: Insight (Emotions) or
Performance (Emoting)
• Gain one dot of Auspex or Blood Sorcery
• Gain the Feeding Merit: Bloodhound (•)
• Gain the Feeding Merit: Reanimated
Emotions (••)
• Gain the Substance Use Flaw: Hopeless
Addiction (••) (Instead of a drug, you are
addicted to resonances; you suffer the
penalty when you do not have a resonance)
• Hunting Pools: Wits + Insight or
Manipulation + Performance. Pick out the one
person in a crowd too deep in their feelings to
resist or incite strong emotions
in an audience
with your performance and pluck the most
affected for a backstage
tasting.

Remote Feeder

The advent of the internet opened up the
keyboard and camera as new feeding mechanisms
for tech­savvy Kindred. You prefer to feed using
the world wide web: you are a streamer with
followers eager to get within fangs­reach of you,
or you hack into blood bank networks, diverting
shipments to refrigerated dead­drops and pilfering
from trucks parked for the night. This feeding
style potentially allows you to funnel blood from
anywhere in the world to your physical location ­
something you use to decrease your chance of
detection. In life, you might have been a content
creator, an IT specialist, or a gamer.
• Add a specialty: Finance (Monetization)
or Technology (Hacking)
• Gain one dot of Presence or Celerity
• Gain the Feeding Merit: Iron Gullet (•••)
or three dots of Haven (•••)
• Gain two dots of Herd (••)
• Gain four dots of Adversary (••••) (the
Camarilla Sheriff, or other Kindred, have made
it their business to stop you from
using
technology to feed)
• Hunting Pools: Manipulation + Finance or
Intelligence + Technology. Fulfill your
Patreon obligations to spend time with (and
feed on) your high­tier patrons or divert
shipments of fractionated plasma to a

refrigerated dead drop of your choice.

Sipper

You have perfected the art of taking the tiniest of
sips from a mortal, feeding a mere lick at a time.
By spending an entire Scene, or longer, feeding on
a crowd in this way, you spread out the impact of
your appetites to minimize harm – and notice – by
any individual. This habit has the unfortunate side
effect of making you unable to feed in larger
volumes; your Beast is adapted to grazing, rather
than glutting (although it may still unwisely
overeat from time to time). In life, you might have
been a health food nut, a nutritionist, or a snack
hound.
• Add a specialty: Stealth (Feeding) or
Athletics (Dodge)
• Gain one dot of Celerity or Dominate
• Gain the Light Stomach Feeding Flaw (••)
• Gain two dots of Contacts (••)
• Gain one dot of Allies (•)
• Hunting Pools: Wits + Stealth or
Dexterity + Athletics. Find somewhere
crowded and start nibbling – you must
either
hide your many bites from view as accidental
contact or amorous club activity
or
successfully dodge the elbows and feet
flying
your way from affronted victims as you blend
back in with the crowd.

Skimmer

You acquire blood through a business that you own
or that employs you; a blood donation center or an
alternative medicine clinic offering bloodletting to
gullible mortals. The business itself does
legitimate work, but you skim blood off the top for
your own uses. Maybe you sneak a little sip from
each bloodletter, or perhaps you doctor records to
conceal missing bags of whole blood. You probably
worked in the healthcare industry in life, whether
on the conventional or alternative side.
• Add a specialty: Stealth (Feeding) or
Athletics (Dodge)
• Gain one dot of Celerity or Dominate
• Gain the Light Stomach Feeding Flaw(••)
• Gain two dots of Contacts (••)
• Hunting Pools: Manipulation + Larceny or
Resolve + Finance. Forge signatures and
fake paperwork to mask your consumption of
blood or do the nitty gritty work of running a
business model that grants you
legal access to
the blood of your patients.

Specimen

The Second Inquisition, Pentex, or another shady
mortal institution has pinned you down as one of
their research subjects like a butterfly in a box.
They grant you more freedom than the butterfly,
but you're probably not convinced they don't plan
to stake you to a table someday. Your research
"partners" provide you with blood and money in
exchange for your willing participation in their
experiments. It's possible that you entered into this
relationship willingly ­ perhaps your sponsors
even have your best interests at heart, or caused
your Embrace during a previous experiment ­ but
it's also possible that you were blackmailed into the
relationship. Either way, you walk a delicate
balance between keeping your blood suppliers
happy and concealing the massive breach of the
Masquerade you perpetuate each night. In life, you
might have been a scientist, a psychologist, a
nurse, or a college student.
• Add one specialty: Science (Biology) or
Subterfuge (Masquerade)
• Gain one dot of Blood Sorcery or
Protean
• Gain three dots of Herd (•••)
• Gain two dots of Resources (••)
• Gain the Dark Secret: Masquerade
Breacher Flaw (••)
• Gain the Known Blankbody Flaw (••)
• Hunting Pools: Intelligence + Science or
Wits + Subterfuge. Aid or participate in
your
sponsor's research or feed them false
information to get your fix.

Spider

You prefer to feed by drawing mortals into your
web... and perhaps only sometimes allowing them
to leave. You own a hotel, a theatre, a club, a
brothel, a bar, or any of a hundred other types of
establishment designed to entice patrons to linger
within. Some Spiders toy with their meals before
dining, cultivating an exquisite experience for
their final moments, while others maintain a façade
of severe authority over their domain designed to
instill a subtle unease among their guests. In life,
you might have been a hotelier, a bartender, a stage
manager, or a Madame.
• Add a specialty: Etiquette (Hospitality) or
Intimidation (Authority)
• Gain one dot of Dominate or Protean
• Gain two dots of Haven or Resources (••)

• Gain one dot of Enemies (•)
• Hunting Pools: Charisma + Etiquette or
Resolve + Intimidation. Draw victims into your
web with your impeccable manners and charm ­
or just scare them stiff.

Stalker

A vampire is either predator or a parasite, and you
most definitely prefer to be a predator. You hunt
your victims, human or not, stalking them through
midnight streets or moonlit glades until the
perfect moment to strike arrives. You savor the
pursuit, drawing it out until the Beast demands
that you wait no longer. As a mortal, you might
have been a big­game hunter, an investigative
journalist, or a detective.
• Add a specialty: Craft (Traps) or Survival
(Tracking)
• Gain one dot of Animalism or Obfuscate
• Gain one dot of Contacts (•)
• Hunting Pools: Intelligence + Craft or
Wits + Survival. Set a trap to catch your prey
or track them by spoor, prints, and scent.

Tampon Sucker

There are millions of mortals in the world that
spend over 10% of their lives bleeding freely. To
your mind, this is a sadly untapped resource – one
you have adapted to use. You rifle through the
trash of public bathrooms to find used menstrual
products from which you can suck dregs of blood
like syrup from a lollipop. As distasteful as some
might consider your diet, you can find sources of
food with ease and impunity; bathrooms are mostly
free of cameras and usually remain deserted in the
deep night you haunt. In life, you might have been
homeless, a freegan, or a radical feminist.
• Add a specialty: Awareness (Blood) or
Survival (Urban)
• Gain one dot of Obfuscate or Protean
• Gain the Iron Gullet Merit (•••) or three
dots of Herd (•••)
• Gain the Shunned Flaw (••) There are
those Kindred who respond with a visceral
disgust to your menstrual diet.
• Hunting Pools: Wits + Awareness or
Dexterity + Survival. Smell nearby menstruation
or the telltale perfume of a lavatory with a
tampon disposal bucket, or navigate to the
closest such buffet with
nothing but your
knowledge of urban planning and a bit of deft
window
climbing.

Therapist

You feed on those with mental illnesses,
particularly suicidality. Maybe you genuinely think
that a sweet, painless death is the best gift you can
give to these people, maybe you get a sick joy from
exploiting their pain, or maybe you just like feeling
completely sated. Some Therapists choose not to
kill their victims, instead using their Kiss to give
them a moment of bliss while they use their words
to encourage them to get them through the next
week ­ and to the Therapist's next meal. If you do
kill your victims, you take pains to make their
deaths look like true suicides, and if you're actually
kindhearted you could even carry out their last
wishes like some sanguine angel of death. In life,
you might have experienced suicidality yourself or
worked as a mental health professional.
• Add a specialty: Insight (Suicidality) or
Academics (Psychology)
• Gain one dot of Auspex or Dominate
• Spend two dots among Contacts, Herd,
and Resources (••)
• Gain the Mythic Flaw: Folkloric Block
(Uninvited Entry) (•) Becoming so attuned to
your victims has caused your blood to
adhere
to their wishes, even when those
wishes are for
you to go away.
• Hunting Pools: Manipulation + Insight or
Charisma + Academics. Play the role of
sympathetic ear to a troubled victim and finish the
vent­sesh with a soothing snack or arrange an
impromptu meeting with one of your more
vulnerable clients.

Warden

You feed on those most powerless to resist you:
prisoners of the law, infirmity, or their own minds.
You've cultivated a flawless cover as a police
officer, prison warden, or nurse that allows you to
feed on a captive population with impunity. You
might have held this position in life, or you might
have been an inmate yourself, taking the advantage
your undeath affords you to get revenge on old
enemies.
• Add a specialty: Melee (Mortals) or
Politics (Regulations)
• Gain one dot of Potence or Obfuscate
• Gain one dot of Contacts or Influence (•)
• Gain two dots of Enemies (••) (former
inmates on whom you once fed, or their
relatives)

• Hunting Pools: Strength + Melee or
Manipulation + Politics. Feed under the guise of
beating down the most likely prisoner or twist
institutional politics to look the other way as you
enter and exit your meal's room.

Xenophile

Changelings, werewolves, mages… these are all
dangerous and evasive prey for vampires of all but
the greatest age and most potent vitae. And yet,
you have developed a taste for their halcyon blood.
When you can, you feed on the blood of other
supernatural creatures in any way that presents
itself, earning yourself both allies and enemies. In
life, you might have been one of the lupine kinfolk,
a minor mage, friend to a changeling, or a fantasy
nerd.
• Add a specialty: Occult (Lupines) or
(Changelings) or (Mages), or Insight (True
Nature)
• Gain one dot of Foritude or Protean
• Gain a four dot Ally (••••) (a supernatural
you help who doesn't mind if you feed on their
enemies)
• Gain a two dot Adversary (••) (a
supernatural who escaped you)
• Gain the Feeding Flaw: Methuselah's
Thirst (•)
• Hunting Pools: Intelligence + Occult or
Wits + Insight. Hunting supernaturals will
always be difficult, but combing through the occult
community or staying alert to those around you
that might have an unusual nature finds you plenty
of likely victims, even if most of your hunts end
without bringing down a lupine, mage, or
changeling.

New Merits and Flaws
Some of the Predator Types described above
reference new Merits and Flaws. Those are
presented here for your use. They can be taken at
character creation like any other Merits and Flaws,
but the Predator Type in which they are first
mentioned is where they feature most prominently.

Reanimated Emotions (Merit)

You are especially attuned to the resonance in your
vitae. Your Frenzy checks are altered depending
on your current resonance:
• Choleric. You gain a 2­dice bonus to
Hunger Frenzy checks, but suffer a 1­die
penalty to Fury Frenzy checks.
• Melancholic. You gain a 2­dice bonus to
Fury Frenzy checks, but suffer a 1­die
penalty to Terror Frenzy checks.
• Phlegmatic. You gain a 1­die bonus to all
Frenzy checks, but suffer a 1­die penalty to Social
tests that do not use Composure.
• Sanguine. You gain a 2­dice bonus to
Terror Frenzy checks, but suffer a 1­die
penalty to Hunger Frenzy checks.

Dependent (Flaw)

You rely on a single mortal for all your blood. If
you feed on any mortal other than your chosen
blood doll, you take a Stain. If your blood doll dies
from something other than your Embrace, you
take two additional Stains. While you do not have
a blood doll, you do not take stains for feeding
from other mortals.

Intermittent Fasting (Flaw)

You strive to feed no more than once per night so
as to limit the burden you impose on the world. If
you feed more than once on a given night, you take
a Stain.

Light Stomach (Flaw)

Your undead body has become accustomed to the
lightest of meals and cannot abide gluttonous
slurping. If you slake more than one Hunger per
scene, your body vomits it up, causing you to make
Rouse Checks equal to the amount of Hunger you
slaked in the scene. You can spend a point of
Willpower to delay this violent expulsion by one
turn per Willpower, but it is ultimately inevitable.

